# Genomic intervals: construction and inspection

This lesson ports the opening `GRanges` construction section and exercises 1-2 from Chapter 6 of [*Computational Genomics with R*](https://compgenomr.github.io/book/operations-on-genomic-intervals-and-genome-arithmetic.html). The source uses one-based, closed coordinates, so width is `end - start + 1`.

## Construct the chapter example

The three rows below are the exact chromosome, start, end, and strand values in the source `createGR` chunk. A BioLang table is the direct tabular equivalent for this introductory section.

```biolang
let gr = table([
    {chrom: "chr1", start: 50, end: 100, strand: "+"},
    {chrom: "chr2", start: 150, end: 200, strand: "-"},
    {chrom: "chr2", start: 200, end: 300, strand: "-"}
])
gr
```

The source immediately selects the first two rows.

```biolang
head(gr, 2)
```

## Attach interval metadata

The source recreates the same coordinates with `names` and `scores`, then appends a second name column. These values are preserved exactly.

```biolang
let annotated = table([
    {chrom: "chr1", start: 50, end: 100, name: "id1", score: 100, name2: "pax6", name3: "A"},
    {chrom: "chr2", start: 150, end: 200, name: "id3", score: 90, name2: "meis1", name3: "C"},
    {chrom: "chr2", start: 200, end: 300, name: "id2", score: 50, name2: "zic4", name3: "B"}
])
annotated
```

## Exercises 1-2

This is the exact exercise table from the chapter.

```biolang
let exercise = table([
    {chrom: "chr1", start: 10000, end: 10300, strand: "+", score: 10},
    {chrom: "chr1", start: 11100, end: 11500, strand: "-", score: 20},
    {chrom: "chr2", start: 20000, end: 20030, strand: "+", score: 15}
])

let inspected = exercise |> map(|row| {
    chrom: row.chrom,
    start: row.start,
    end: row.end,
    strand: row.strand,
    width: row.end - row.start + 1
})
inspected
```

```biolang
let plus_strand = exercise |> filter(|row| row.strand == "+")
let chromosome_1 = exercise |> filter(|row| row.chrom == "chr1")
{plus_strand: plus_strand, chromosome_1: chromosome_1}
```

```biolang
assert nrow(gr) == 3, "the source example has three intervals"
assert inspected[0].width == 301, "closed interval 10000-10300 has width 301"
assert inspected[1].width == 401, "closed interval 11100-11500 has width 401"
assert inspected[2].width == 31, "closed interval 20000-20030 has width 31"
assert nrow(plus_strand) == 2, "two exercise intervals are on the plus strand"
assert nrow(chromosome_1) == 2, "two exercise intervals are on chromosome 1"
"All source-value checks passed."
```
